; Regression sentinel for bug #184 (cross-block carry chain).
;
; Bug #184: when an i32 (or wider) negation lowers to a SubSetCarry chain
; that splits across basic blocks (e.g. an i32 PHI accumulator → neg →
; select i32 → store), the borrow flag CC.C is silently clobbered by any
; CC-touching MI between bb.5's last SBC and bb.9's first SBC.
;
; The wrong code computed `0x0000FFDF` for `atol_like("-3")` (top 2 bytes
; should be 0xFF, propagated from sign extension of the borrow chain).
; USim trace pinned the clobber to the `cmpb #$2d` (the is_neg=='-' check)
; that sits between bb.5 and bb.9.
;
; Fix: at instruction selection time, when the carry-in to a
; SubSetCarryUse-family consumer is a phantom-BIT1 producer in a DIFFERENT
; basic block, freeze CC.C into a byte right after the producer (via
; `MaterializeCarryToByte_i8`) and restore CC.C right before the consumer
; (via the new `MaterializeByteToCarry_i8` pseudo, which expands to a
; single LSRB). The byte vreg crosses blocks naturally as a regular ABc
; value.
;
; This codegen sentinel locks the shape produced for atol_like at -O0 —
; specifically the materialise/restore pair around the cond trampolines.
; The companion execution test is `test/MC/MC6809/Execution/codegen-picolibc.s`
; (via test_atol_w in codegen-picolibc.ll) which actually runs on usim
; and verifies the bytes. This .ll is the durable shape sentinel.

